The first series of ''[[The Celebrity Traitors]]'' began airing on 8 October 2025 on [[BBC One]]. It was presented by [[Claudia Winkleman]], with [[Ed Gamble]] fronting the companion show ''[[The Traitors: Uncloaked|The Celebrity Traitors: Uncloaked]]''.

The series concluded on 6 November 2025, when [[Alan Carr]] won the series as the last remaining Traitor, ultimately winning £87,500 for his chosen charity Neuroblastoma UK.

The series was the most watched show of the year on UK television,<ref>{{Cite web |last=Kanter |first=Jake |date=2026-01-05 |title=British TV’s Most-Watched In 2025: ‘Celebrity Traitors’ Imperious; ‘Adolescence’ Tops Streaming; Plus ‘KPop Demon Hunters’ Monster Success |url=https://deadline.com/2026/01/2025-most-watched-celebrity-traitors-kpop-demon-hunters-1236663712/ |access-date=2026-09-18 |website=Deadline |language=en-US}}</ref> and the series finale was [[List of most watched television broadcasts in the United Kingdom|the most watched UK television broadcast of 2025]].<ref>{{Cite web |title=Weekly top 50 programmes – As Viewed (Jan 2024 – Dec 2025) Barb |url=https://www.barb.co.uk/viewing-data/as-viewed-top-50/ |access-date=2026-05-08 |language=en-GB}}</ref> It is widely considered to be one of the best television shows of the year.<ref>{{Cite news |last=Samadder |first=Rhik |date=2025-12-19 |title=The 50 best TV shows of 2025: No 3 – The Celebrity Traitors |url=https://www.theguardian.com/tv-and-radio/2025/dec/19/the-50-best-tv-shows-of-2025-no-3-the-celebrity-traitors |access-date=2026-09-18 |work=The Guardian |language=en-GB |issn=0261-3077}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Bryan |first=Scott |date=2025-11-07 |title=‘Celebrity Traitors U.K.’: Why the British Show’s First Star-Studded Season Made for the Best Reality TV of the Year |url=https://variety.com/2025/tv/columns/celebrity-traitors-uk-review-star-spinoff-best-reality-tv-year-1236572303/ |access-date=2026-09-19 |website=Variety |language=en-US}}</ref> The series received various awards, most notably two [[British Academy Television Awards]] (including one for Alan Carr winning), two [[British Academy Television Craft Awards]], and one [[National Television Award]] (and contributed to Alan Carr winning the [[National Television Award for Special Recognition]] in 2026).<ref>{{Cite web |date=2026-09-08 |title=Alan Carr gets tearful at NTAs as he's honoured with Special Recognition by Celebrity Traitors stars |url=https://www.digitalspy.com/tv/a73644620/special-recognition-ntas-2026-alan-carr/ |access-date=2026-09-18 |website=Digital Spy |language=en-GB}}</ref>

==Production==
In August 2024, the [[BBC]] confirmed that ''The Celebrity Traitors'' had been commissioned, along with two more series of ''The Traitors'', [[The Traitors (British TV series) series 3|the first of which]] aired in January 2025.<ref>{{cite web |title=The Traitors: First UK celebrity series announced |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c70j84rvg91o |website=[[BBC News]] |accessdate=13 May 2025 |language=en-gb |date=22 August 2024}}</ref> Speaking at the [[Edinburgh International Television Festival]], Kalpna Patel-Knight, the BBC's head of entertainment, said: "''The Traitors'' has well and truly established itself as an unmissable highlight of the year and the news of a fourth outing, alongside a brand new celebrity version coming to the BBC, will take the series to a whole new level.<ref>{{cite web |last1=Creamer |first1=Jon |title=Traitors confirmed for S4 plus celeb version |url=https://www.televisual.com/news/traitors-confirmed-for-s4-plus-celeb-version/ |website=Televisual |accessdate=13 May 2025 |date=22 August 2024 |archive-date=15 May 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250515170306/https://www.televisual.com/news/traitors-confirmed-for-s4-plus-celeb-version/ |url-status=live }}</ref> In April 2025, it was confirmed that the show would air in the autumn of that year,<ref>{{cite web |title=BBC's Celebrity Traitors gets exciting update ahead of its 2025 release |url=https://www.digitalspy.com/tv/reality-tv/a64349830/celebrity-traitors-release-window/ |website=[[Digital Spy]] |accessdate=14 May 2025 |date=1 April 2025 |archive-date=15 May 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250515170305/https://www.digitalspy.com/tv/reality-tv/a64349830/celebrity-traitors-release-window/ |url-status=live }}</ref> with October 2025 later specified.<ref>{{Cite web |title=The Celebrity Traitors - Everything you need to know |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/mediacentre/articles/2025/the-celebrity-traitors |access-date=2025-08-21 |website=www.bbc.co.uk |language=en-GB |archive-date=14 May 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250514221454/https://www.bbc.co.uk/mediacentre/articles/2025/the-celebrity-traitors |url-status=live }}</ref>

Filming for the series began on 22 April 2025 at [[Ardross, Highland|Ardross Castle]] and concluded the following month, consisting of 9 episodes due to air over four weeks from 8 October to 6 November 2025.<ref>{{cite web |title=The Celebrity Traitors launch date confirmed and fans will be treated to an extra-long opening episode |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/mediacentre/2025/celebrity-traitors-launch-date-confirmed |website=BBC |format=press release |access-date=21 September 2025 |archive-date=21 September 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250921002202/https://www.bbc.co.uk/mediacentre/2025/celebrity-traitors-launch-date-confirmed |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{cite web |last1=Ross |first1=Charley |title=When does Celebrity Traitors start? Here's what we know |url=https://www.glamourmagazine.co.uk/article/when-does-celebrity-traitors-start |website=Glamour UK |accessdate=14 May 2025 |date=25 April 2025 |archive-date=27 April 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250427202318/https://www.glamourmagazine.co.uk/article/when-does-celebrity-traitors-start |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{cite web |title=Celebrity Traitors latest: Release date, cast and filming revealed |url=https://www.heart.co.uk/showbiz/celebrity-traitors-start-date-line-up/ |website=[[Heart (radio network)|Heart]] |accessdate=14 May 2025 |language=en |archive-date=15 May 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250515170305/https://www.heart.co.uk/showbiz/celebrity-traitors-start-date-line-up/ |url-status=live }}</ref> Following the cast announcement, host [[Claudia Winkleman]] said "We're incredibly lucky these brilliant people have said yes. I’d love to say we'll take it easy on them, and they'll just wander round the castle and eat toast for a couple of weeks - but that would be a lie."<ref>{{cite web |title=The BBC's 'Celebrity Traitors' Cast Pits an Olympian Against a 'Ted Lasso' Star |url=https://www.cosmopolitan.com/entertainment/tv/g64759984/celebrity-traitors-cast-line-up-contestants-bbc/ |website=Cosmopolitan |accessdate=14 May 2025 |date=13 May 2025 |archive-date=14 May 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250514120833/https://www.cosmopolitan.com/entertainment/tv/g64759984/celebrity-traitors-cast-line-up-contestants-bbc/ |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{cite web |title=The Celebrity Traitors' "brilliant" cast has officially been confirmed – along with a release date window |url=https://www.digitalspy.com/tv/reality-tv/a64757349/the-celebrity-traitors-cast-release-window/ |website=[[Digital Spy]] |accessdate=14 May 2025 |date=13 May 2025 |archive-date=13 May 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250513182707/https://www.digitalspy.com/tv/reality-tv/a64757349/the-celebrity-traitors-cast-release-window/ |url-status=live }}</ref>

The final episode of the series was mistakenly released early online in Canada and New Zealand as the episode was mistakenly made available on the [[Crave (streaming service)|Crave]] and [[ThreeNow]] streaming services 24 hours in advance of its broadcast on BBC One, due to a miscommunication between [[All3Media|All3Media International]] and its international partners.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://deadline.com/2025/11/celebrity-traitors-uk-leak-canada-all3media-reviewing-processes-1236610470/|title='Celebrity Traitors UK' Distributor All3Media International “Urgently Reviewing Our Processes” After Dramatic Finale Leaks A Day Early In Canada & New Zealand|first=Max|last=Goldbart|date=7 November 2025|accessdate=18 November 2025|archive-date=9 November 2025|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20251109123601/https://deadline.com/2025/11/celebrity-traitors-uk-leak-canada-all3media-reviewing-processes-1236610470/|url-status=live}}</ref>

== Contestants ==
The 19 celebrities competing in the series were revealed on 13 May 2025.<ref>{{cite web |title=Celebrity Traitors line-up confirmed: Stephen Fry, Paloma Faith, Alan Carr and more |url=https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cx2enyjk407o |website=[[BBC News]] |accessdate=14 May 2025 |date=13 May 2025 |archive-date=14 May 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250514032720/https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cx2enyjk407o |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{cite web |title=Celebrity Traitors line-up officially confirmed – including Taskmaster and Thursday Murder Club stars {{!}} Radio Times |url=https://www.radiotimes.com/tv/entertainment/reality-tv/celebrity-traitors-line-up-officially-confirmed-newsupdate/ |website=[[Radio Times]] |accessdate=14 May 2025}}</ref> Their chosen charities were not revealed until after the show had concluded, with the winner's charity named in the final.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://goss.ie/realitytv/bbc-reveals-names-of-19-charities-that-stars-were-playing-for-during-the-celebrity-traitors-443331|title=BBC reveals names of 19 charities that stars were playing for during The Celebrity Traitors|date=14 November 2025|accessdate=18 November 2025}}</ref>

