==Reception==
===Critical reception===

The series received critical acclaim. It was praised for its casting of “actually recognisable names” by ''[[The Independent]]'',<ref>{{Cite web |date=2025-10-09 |title=Celebrity Traitors viewers hail nervous contestant highlight of new series |url=https://www.the-independent.com/arts-entertainment/tv/news/celebrity-traitors-alan-carr-bbc-b2842142.html |access-date=2026-05-08 |website=The Independent |language=en}}</ref> with particular praise for its casting of Alan Carr with ''[[HuffPost]]'' saying that he “stole the show”. Alan Carr winning was dubbed the “TV moment of the year” by ''[[The i Paper]]'',<ref>{{Cite web |last=Baker |first=Emily |date=2025-11-07 |title=The Celebrity Traitors final delivered the TV moment of the year |url=https://inews.co.uk/culture/television/celebrity-traitors-final-best-tv-ever-seen-4021061 |access-date=2026-05-08 |website=The i Paper |language=en-US}}</ref> and one of the “most unifying cultural moments” of the century in the UK.<ref>{{Cite web 
|last=Edwards |first=Laura |last2=Swain |first2=Izzy
|date=2026-09-18 |title=Alan Carr's Celebrity Traitors win ranks among Britain's top unifying cultural moments   |url=https://www.lincolnshirelive.co.uk/news/uk-world-news/celebrity-traitors-finale-queen-tendendo-11160876 |access-date=2026-09-18 |website=www.lincolnshirelive.co.uk}}</ref> 

